  "term": "chloride channel",
  "definition": "A chloride channel is a cell membrane pathway that allows chloride ions to move across the membrane when the channel is activated. In this packet, chloride channels are described in relation to GABA A receptors, where their activation produces measurable transmembrane chloride currents.",
